{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 15ba7c26: Explore does not predict the physical\nadmission of the turn. I withdraw the second test of 04218678.\n\n1. Section 5.1 of the note bounds the contract: the exploration and\n   the scope's judgment derive equal consequences, and the record\n   also checks the envelope and the authority at the commit. The\n   turn's `fits` and `capacityFull` checks are of that second kind.\n   They need the bytes of the real entry, which no act holds.\n2. So an admitted exploration is the judge's answer. It is not a\n   promise that the scope has room. The scope can still refuse\n   `scope-full` at the commit. Add no capacity input and no shared\n   admission primitive to Explore. Copy no runtime admission into\n   `packages/client`.\n3. Invariant 9 compares an exploration with the scope's judgment.\n   A turn that the scope refuses before or after the judge, for\n   room, is outside the comparison. The suite states that rule in\n   one place.\n4. The first test of 04218678 stands: the record count and the\n   reservations of the hypothetical view equal the scope's state\n   after the real submit.\n5. In place of the second test, the E1 note states the boundary in\n   two sentences. A page reads room from the counts and bounds\n   that Observe gives, as section 5.5 says.\n\nI amend section 5.1 of the note with this boundary, beside the\namendments of ruling fa103f71.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:15ba7c264deb57f68170bd95be636a982eedfe5f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02c1227e7dc1c04a96ab423dd34c58537b63a2f2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03c2d3b4bab05912804bc48129712cd98f805758, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06d96cd732ff547fa8959619d6df87c5953f2ded, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d76705dfdd74d8de0047a7a257da83b75d575e2 and 73 more","to":"feb90d3